  '**The inspectorate holds that the tolerance of the recording instrument belongs to the instrument and not to the product.** **On his account a reading at the stated limit is compliant, because the instrument may be reading half a degree high, and an excursion begins only above the limit plus that half degree.** **For him the manufacturer\'s insert is a commercial document and carries no authority in a registration file.**',
  '**The manufacturer holds that the tolerance belongs to the product.** **On that account a reading at the stated limit has already exceeded what the product will bear, because the product was specified against a true temperature and not against an instrument.** **The same objection applies, as he has it, to every reading taken at the door of the cabinet rather than at the shelf.**',
