out.push(A('**1** _…about **anything** that has been measured._   **2** _…On this view, the refusal is itself the selection._ ⚠ **Delete _he says_: the marker already carries the attribution and a verb after it reopens the question.**   **3** _Both reviewers **were** not persuaded…_   **4** _Where Haddad reads the fall as seasonal, Mansour reads it as a trend._ ⚠ **Delete _but_: _where_ has already joined the two halves.**   **5** _…the only one that assumes **no** mathematics._   **6** _A difference of ground is **settled** by naming what would distinguish the two._'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **Four usable findings and one request.** **The question cannot be answered as asked, because three of the four are right and the fourth is answering a different question** — **so the room gives her what all four agree about, with the figure once; the one dispute, with the document that would settle it and the name of whoever holds it; the pairing that is not a dispute and looks most like one; and a refusal of the ranking with a reason.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the eighth mediation and the first in which the reader\'s question is refused outright, so the refusal has to be taught with its replacement attached or the class will learn evasion.** **A refusal with nothing beside it is the answer Mrs Tarabishi gave first and it was no use on Thursday.** **Four findings and one request is a decision, and a reader handed a decision stops asking for a ranking.** ⚠ **Say the refusal flat.** _I have no basis for preferring one of them to the other._ **Stress on _no_ makes it a refusal and the reader hears evasion; flat, it is a statement of what the evidence will carry** — **and the sentence after it has to be the request, immediately, or the flatness is wasted.** **Drill the two sentences as a pair.**'));
