out.push(SAMPLE(['Asked which of the four is right, Mrs Tarabishi said the honest answer is that three of them are right and the fourth is answering a different question, which is no use to the director at all on Thursday. Mrs Khoury said it is no use because it is an answer to the question she asked, and she asked the wrong question and is entitled to: she has four papers and ten minutes, and sorting them is the work she is paying somebody else to do. Dr Qabbani asked what goes in front of her, and the four things the four of them agree about, first, with the figure stated once; then the one dispute, named, with the document that would settle it and the name of whoever holds it; then the pairing that is not a dispute at all and looks most like one. Mr Shihabi said that is Khalil against the other three, and Mrs Oueidat said Khalil is 8.1, a difference of subject: the other three are counting repayment and he is counting exclusion, and a director who thinks he is disagreeing with them will discount him when he is the only one of the four who has told her anything about the people who did not get a loan. Mr Tayara asked about Haddad against Mansour, and that is the dispute, and it is 8.2: they agree about every number and differ about the ground, and it is settled by the records of the refused applicants, which exist and are not published, and the agency the director works for holds them. Mrs Ajouz said so the answer to her question is a request, and Mrs Khoury said the answer is four usable findings and one request, and the request is nine words long and she can grant it on Thursday. Mrs Rizk asked what you refuse to put in front of her, and a ranking: she would act on it, and it would be Mrs Tarabishi\'s temperament with four names underneath it. Mr Attar asked whether she does not simply ask again, and Mrs Oueidat said she asks once more and then stops, because what she wants is a decision and not a ranking. Mr Zahreddine said the tribunal does the same with two engineers, and Mrs Khoury said every reader of a disagreement does, and the request to rank is not dishonest: it is what a reader asks for when they have been given a disagreement and no arithmetic. Mr Tayara asked about Darwish, and Darwish agrees with both and settles neither, which sounds like a wasted paper and is the most useful of the four. And Mrs Tarabishi said the thing she will take away is the six pairings: she spent two years reading four authors as four opinions, and they are six relationships, of which one is a disagreement and five are information.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **Mrs Tarabishi\'s closing sentence is the one to carry out of the unit.** **She spent two years reading four authors as four opinions, and they are six relationships, of which one is a disagreement and five are information.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ _On balance I prefer Haddad._ → **a ranking with no basis, which the reader will act on.**   **2** _The evidence is mixed._ → **the sentence that costs nothing and says nothing.** **Give the six labels.**   **3** _The question remains open._ → ⚠ **true, and not an answer.** **Name the document and whoever holds it.**   **4** _Khalil disagrees with the other three._ → **he is answering a different question**, and a reader told he disagrees will discount the only writer who has said anything about the people who were refused.'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read – exam practice (Reading and Use of English Part 6)'));
out.push(A('**1** **D**   **2** **A**   **3** **B**   **4** **C**'));
out.push(A('⚠ **1 is D.** **A, B and C all say a reviewer should not adjudicate; D holds that where the published evidence settles a question the reviewer who refuses to say so _has written a bibliography and called it a review_.**   **2 is A.** **C calls the measuring-different-things finding the most useful service a review performs, and B and D agree with C.** **A alone says the phrase _is now doing a great deal of work that it has not earned_.**   **3 is B.** **A, C and D all print an unsettleable dispute as unsettleable; B holds that _unresolved_ does active harm and that the two predictions should be printed instead.**   **4 is C.** **B calls naming the measurement the chief reason for writing a review; A and D agree; C alone holds that a reviewer who specifies the study _has become a proposer_.**'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Part 6 is new at C1 and has no equivalent at B2, and the thing to teach is the reading order and not the questions.** **Read all four extracts before answering anything**, and build a four-by-four grid on paper: the four writers down the side and the four issues across the top. **Each question then reads off one column.** **A candidate who answers question 1 after reading extract A has already lost the part**, because every question in it is comparative. ⚠ **And warn the room about the half they will find harder.** **About half the marks in this part are on writers who _share_ a view, and two writers who agree almost never agree in the same words** — **which is 8.1\'s finding arriving in the examination, and the reason candidates who match wording rather than position score badly here.**'));
